00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.089
So we spoke earlier.

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:08.089
A Trump second impeachment trial is over.

00:00:08.089 --> 00:00:09.089
He's been acquitted exactly as we predicted.

00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:10.089
I was expecting five Republicans to vote guilty.

00:00:10.089 --> 00:00:11.089
We got seven.

00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:12.519
That's something, but still not the sixty
seven that were required to convict.

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:17.530
Now, with impeachment out of the way and not
that this should have delayed covid relief

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:21.580
anyway, but now with impeachment out of the
way, no more excuses.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.199
It's time to get covid relief done.

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:29.380
Now, I am already to be very clear, I think
Joe Biden's been doing a good job so far.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.911
I like how much he's gotten done and how quickly
he has got it done.

00:00:31.911 --> 00:00:37.610
Joe Biden did say checks going out right away
when I'm sworn in.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.910
If we have the two Senate seats, Democrats
have the two Senate seats, we're getting close

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:48.450
to a month and we're still dealing with how
exactly is this stimulus bill going to pass?

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:53.579
It is increasingly and abundantly clear that
at least in the lead up, Republicans aren't

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:54.579
going to play ball.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:01:01.789
Now, I've said before, I think that the political
risk of voting no on the stimulus bill is

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:05.350
too great for all Republicans to vote no.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:10.560
I believe that if Democrats move forward with
passing the covid stimulus package, one point

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.579
nine dollars billion via budget reconciliation,
which requires only a simple majority, meaning

00:01:15.579 --> 00:01:17.909
they can do it with fifty senators.

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:20.460
And Kamala Harris is a tie breaking vote votes.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.969
I believe that if that's the way to do it,
they should do it.

00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:24.149
This is too important.

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:27.310
And it was Joe Biden's promise, after all.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:33.270
But I think he will get some Republicans who
go who go for it because many of the same

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:39.799
Republicans who voted guilty for Trump in
the second impeachment trial have more moderate

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:47.000
constituencies and or don't care so much about
being seen as sticking with the Republicans

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.600
and being on the team.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.579
I think it's quite plausible Mitt Romney would
go for it.

00:01:51.579 --> 00:01:56.299
Susan Collins, Lisa Murkowski, Ben Sasse,
Pat Toomey, a lot of the same people who voted

00:01:56.299 --> 00:02:01.170
guilty on Saturday for Donald Trump, I think
ultimately will come around because they realize

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:04.069
that this is actually what their constituents
want.

00:02:04.069 --> 00:02:09.220
So there's a New York Times article which
says the Biden agenda now with now with impeachment

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:15.200
out of the way, the Biden agenda takes center
stage and that the order, the priorities will

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.709
be passing the one point nine trillion dollar
stimulus bill and then doing green infrastructure

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:24.110
and then doing immigration and then doing
climate change and starting to go through

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.110
this list.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.349
Now, that's probably 18 months of stuff.

00:02:27.349 --> 00:02:30.239
We have to be realistic about how quickly,
you know, maybe a year.

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:35.150
It's not clear, but we just have to get the
covid relief bill done.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:38.019
It's very clear that that is the next step.

00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:42.909
It's very clear that Joe Biden is now risking
failing on a major campaign promise.

00:02:42.909 --> 00:02:46.640
You can you can argue that he already failed
in the sense that he said it would happen

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.640
right away.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.609
And it's been a month since he initially said
it'd be two thousand dollar checks.

00:02:50.609 --> 00:02:54.220
Then it was well, it'll be fourteen hundred
to get to the total of two thousand.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.140
OK, some are defending that.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.140
Some are not.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.750
Some are saying it's a flip flop.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.650
Regardless, we're almost a month in.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:01.790
It's time to do it.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:09.140
And so the report from The New York Times
says that this is now the priority and that

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.189
Joe Biden and Democrats are willing to go
it alone.

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:13.950
What has changed over the last two weeks?

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:14.950
Nothing.

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.579
Joe Biden brought Republicans to the White
House.

00:03:17.579 --> 00:03:18.810
They wanted a plan.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.160
That was it was humiliatingly small.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:26.099
It was a micro plan, I would call it, and
it was less than one third the size of what

00:03:26.099 --> 00:03:28.049
Joe Biden and Democrats want.

00:03:28.049 --> 00:03:30.989
You're negotiating with people who are negotiating
in bad faith.

00:03:30.989 --> 00:03:33.530
They're negotiating down down to something
that's pathetic.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:35.530
It's peanuts for what we need.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:36.530
Just do it.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.340
It's time to get it done.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:43.849
And we will we will soon see whether Joe Biden
understands the limits of so-called unity

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:45.390
and the limits of bipartisanship.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:52.359
And as Jen Psaki Psaki now I know, as Jen
Psaki said many times now, bipartisanship

00:03:52.359 --> 00:03:57.290
doesn't mean that you unite Republicans and
Democrats into one party.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.939
Democrats say one point nine trillion.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:05.140
And it includes the you know, it includes
the payments that we've outlined before in

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:10.060
terms of payments to individuals, payments
for children, business stimulus, enhanced

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:13.290
unemployment, money for vaccine, all these
different things.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:17.079
Republicans want something so dramatically
different that there's really no way to negotiate

00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:19.109
to anything that would make sense.

00:04:19.109 --> 00:04:25.009
The American people are overwhelmingly on
the side of Joe Biden and Democrats, not everybody

00:04:25.009 --> 00:04:26.569
but Signior.

00:04:26.569 --> 00:04:31.500
Support for the one point nine dollars billion
package, so it's just time to pass it and

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.660
this would be a major accomplishment for Joe
Biden.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.210
My expectation would be that as high as Joe
Biden's approval rating is right now and it's

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:47.150
the highest initial job approval of any president
since Bill Clinton in 1993, over twenty eight

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:48.150
years.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:53.249
Right now, this is the highest initial approval
rating of any president dating back 28 years.

00:04:53.249 --> 00:04:58.130
I think it goes higher if Joe Biden is able
to get this done in the next 10 days.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.940
And if not, it will start to be a drag on
him politically.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.430
Politics aside, we need to do it for the economy.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.190
We need to do it for people.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:13.190
And I remain cautiously optimistic that in
the next seven to 10 days, there will be progress.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:18.020
We'll see what is said about it at this week's
press briefings with Jen Psaki, which, of

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.240
course, we'll be covering on YouTube, Twitch
and Faceboo

